 "source": "<!-- Sibling sections with bodies: the blank a section swallows at its end. -->\n\n# Document title\n\nAn opening paragraph, so the first section has a body and not just its\nheading.\n\n## First section\n\nA paragraph whose trailing blank line falls inside this section's byte\nrange rather than between the two sections.\n\n## Second section\n\n### A deeper heading\n\nThe blank before this one is swallowed by the paragraph's own section.\n\n## Third section, entered with no blank line above its body\nProse starting on the very next line.\n\n## Fourth section\n\nA section that ends in a fenced block rather than a paragraph.\n\n```sh\necho done\n```\n\n## Fifth section\n\n- a list, which is the other thing a section can end with\n- second item\n\n## Sixth section\n\n> and a block quote, whose continuation marker also ends a section\n\n## Seventh section\n\n#### A jump from h2 to h4, so the nesting is not one level per heading\n\n##### And back down again, with no body between them\n\nText closing the document.\n",
